{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1572262318,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MTMyNDkxNzQ=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3836","origin":"github"},"title":"get broke reporting on 'notneeded' subdatasets in 0.12.0rc6","message":"Installing an already existing subdataset used to yield a \"notneeded\" result (as `get` does). With 0.12.0rc6 there's no result at all (which as a result breaks datalad-neuroimaging test helper for example dicom datasets:\n\n```\n❱ datalad create some\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/some\ncreate(ok): /tmp/some (dataset)                                                                                              \n(hirni-test-rc6) bpoldrack@brainbfast in /tmp\n❱ cd some\n(hirni-test-rc6) bpoldrack@brainbfast in /tmp/some on git:master\n❱ datalad create -d . nested\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/some/nested\ncreate(ok): nested (dataset)                                                                                                 \naction summary:\n  add (ok: 2)\n  create (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n(hirni-test-rc6) bpoldrack@brainbfast in /tmp/some on git:master\n❱ datalad status\n(hirni-test-rc6) bpoldrack@brainbfast in /tmp/some on git:master\n❱ datalad -f json_pp get nested\n{\n  \"action\": \"get\",\n  \"path\": \"/tmp/some/nested\",\n  \"refds\": \"/tmp/some\",\n  \"status\": \"notneeded\",\n  \"type\": \"directory\"\n}\n(hirni-test-rc6) bpoldrack@brainbfast in /tmp/some on git:master\n❱ datalad -f json_pp install nested\n(hirni-test-rc6) bpoldrack@brainbfast in /tmp/some on git:master\n❱\n```\n\nFrom the diff of `install` itself the change seems to be not in there, which suggests it's actually `get`. However, `get` does yield the correct result, so I'm not yet clear, where it goes wrong. Does that ring a bell, @mih?","files":null}]}